    "enrolment_precedes_registration": true,
    "server_assigns_device_id": true,
    "client_device_id_is_local_until_rebind": true,
    "fingerprint_compared_before_rebind": true,
    "rebind_generates_no_new_key_material": true,
    "rebind_writes_before_deleting": true,
    "rationale": "POST /api/v1/devices carries the public key in its body, so the pair must exist before registration; the server then derives the device id and ignores any the client proposes, while enrolment binds the stored key to a device id in both the record key and the authenticated AAD. Re-enrolling under the assigned id would generate a different pair, leaving the registered fingerprint pointing at a key this browser no longer holds and every workspace envelope later provisioned to the device undecryptable. The same private key is therefore re-protected under the new AAD, write-then-delete so an interruption cannot destroy the only copy."
  },
